        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(channels): share durable ingress monitor",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSix channel integrations maintained parallel copies of durable-ingress scheduling, claim validation, retry, retention, and shutdown bookkeeping. Those copies had begun to drift, making lifecycle fixes easy to miss in one transport and expensive to prove consistently.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMigrates Telegram, WhatsApp, Feishu, QQBot, ZaloUser, and Nostr onto `createChannelIngressMonitor`, with one commit per channel. The shared monitor now owns the common pump, claim identity/version validation, lifecycle fan-out, retention, activity, and stop/idle behavior while each channel retains its transport and delivery contracts.\n\nThe migration deliberately leaves non-isomorphic ownership local: Telegram keeps durable spool admission and offset advancement; WhatsApp keeps prepared-context admission; Feishu keeps broadcast settlement; ZaloUser keeps its deferred-claim abort ledger; Nostr keeps relay admission gates and cursor advancement. QQBot is a clean shared-monitor fit.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Durable inbound delivery retains each channel's existing capacity, TTL, retry, acknowledgement, ordering, and shutdown semantics, with less duplicated lifecycle code.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 603 distinct focused tests passed on Blacksmith Testbox across all six channel surfaces and the shared ingress monitor/drain.\n- Feishu's two fixed-port webhook suites passed in isolated shards; selecting them concurrently reproduced their existing `EADDRINUSE` harness collision even though all assertions passed.\n- `pnpm deadcode:dependencies`, `pnpm deadcode:unused-files`, and `pnpm deadcode:exports` passed.\n- Changed typecheck/lint/format/plugin-SDK gates passed, including the generated plugin SDK API baseline check.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Mandatory branch autoreview against `origin/main` completed clean after adding regressions for both late-redrain shutdown races.\n",
